  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has a sequence AAA of NNN integers such that ∣Ai∣≤1|A_i| \\leq 1∣Ai​∣≤1.\n\nFor each xxx such that −N≤x≤N-N \\leq x \\leq N−N≤x≤N, find the number of non-empty subsequences of AAA whose sum of elements is xxx. Since that answer may be too large, print this modulo 163,577,857163,577,857163,577,857.\n\n###Input:\n\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n###Output:\r\nOutput 2N+12N+12N+1 space-separated integers C0,C1…C2∗NC_0, C_1 \\ldots C_{2*N}C0​,C1​…C2∗N​, where CiC_iCi​ denotes the number of non-empty subsequences with sum (i−N)(i-N)(i−N), modulo 163,577,857163,577,857163,577,857.\n\n###Constraints:\n\n\n1≤T≤1051 \\le T \\le 10^51≤T≤105\n1≤N≤1051 \\le N \\le 10^51≤N≤105\n∣Ai∣≤1|A_i| \\le 1∣Ai​∣≤1 for each valid iii\nIt's guaranteed that the total length of the arrays in one test file doesn't exceed 2∗1062*10^62∗106\n###Sample Input:\n\n`2\r\n2\r\n1 0\r\n3\r\n-1 1 -1\n`###Sample Output:\n\n`0 0 1 2 0\r\n0 1 3 2 1 0 0\n`Explanation:In the first test case, the non-empty subsequences with sum 000 are {0}\\{0\\}{0} while the subsequences with sum 111 are {1}\\{1\\}{1} and {1,0}\\{1,0\\}{1,0}.",
